  "nl_text": "The rschema_0436 database is designed to manage a website's content and user interactions. It consists of nine tables, each representing a distinct entity within the website's structure. The administrator table stores information about the website's administrators, including their unique identifiers, usernames, passwords, emails, creation and update times, and serves as the primary key for the database. The news_article table contains details about published articles, such as their titles, content, authors, publication times, categories, tags, creation and update times, and is identified by a unique article_id. The website_information table holds information about the website itself, including its name, logo, copyright details, creation and update times, and is identified by a unique website_id. The member table stores user account information, including unique identifiers, usernames, passwords, emails, registration times, and update times, and serves as the primary key for the database. The advertisement table contains details about advertisements, including their titles, content, publication times, creation and update times, and is identified by a unique advertisement_id. The message table stores user comments and replies to articles, including the user's unique identifier, the article being commented on, the comment content, the time of posting, and the reply content, and is identified by a unique message_id. The administrator_publish_news table tracks which administrators are responsible for publishing which articles, linking administrators to articles through their unique identifiers. The administrator_manage_advertisement table tracks which administrators are responsible for managing which advertisements, linking administrators to advertisements through their unique identifiers. Finally, the user_message table tracks which users have commented on which messages, linking users to messages through their unique identifiers.",
  "gold_question": "Functional description of news management system\n\nAdministrator functions:\n1. News article entry: Administrators can enter new news articles, including title, content, author, release time, etc.\n2. News article management: Administrators can edit, delete, classify, label, and other operations on published news articles.\n3. Website information settings: Administrators can set basic information of the website, such as name, logo, copyright information, etc.\n4. Member information management: Administrators can manage the website's member information, including adding, deleting, modifying, and checking member information.\n5. Advertising management: Administrators can publish, edit, and delete advertisements.\n6. Message management: Administrators can view, reply to, and delete users' messages under news articles.\n\nUser functions:\n1. Registration and login: Users can access the website through the registration and login functions.\n2. News information query: Users can query and view news information on the website.\n3. Post comments: Users can post comments under news articles.\n4. Search function: Users can search for specific news articles through the search function.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0436.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0436\nCREATE TABLE `administrator` (\n  `admin_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`admin_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `news_article` (\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `publication_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `tags` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`article_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `news_article_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `administrator` (`admin_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `website_information` (\n  `website_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `logo` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `copyright` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`website_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `member` (\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`member_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `advertisement` (\n  `advertisement_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `publication_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`advertisement_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `message` (\n  `message_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `posted_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `reply_content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`message_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `message_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `message_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`article_id`) REFERENCES `news_article` (`article_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `administrator_publish_news` (\n  `admin_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`admin_id`, `article_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `administrator_publish_news_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`admin_id`) REFERENCES `administrator` (`admin_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `administrator_publish_news_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`article_id`) REFERENCES `news_article` (`article_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `administrator_manage_advertisement` (\n  `admin_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `advertisement_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`admin_id`, `advertisement_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `administrator_manage_advertisement_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`admin_id`) REFERENCES `administrator` (`admin_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `administrator_manage_advertisement_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`advertisement_id`) REFERENCES `advertisement` (`advertisement_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_message` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `message_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `message_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_message_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_message_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`message_id`) REFERENCES `message` (`message_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
